# priority.csv — COF Order IDs (SAP Vbeln) to bid FIRST
#
# When a bid window opens (:15 / :45 IST), matched orders whose Vbeln
# (COF Order ID) appears below will be pushed to the FRONT of the
# submit plan — before any non-priority order — so they hit SAP within
# the first ~300 ms of the window.
#
# Format:
#   • One Vbeln per line (numeric string as SAP shows it), OR
#   • CSV with a header row containing "Vbeln" or "COF Order ID"
#
# Rules:
#   • Blank lines and lines starting with "#" are ignored.
#   • Vbelns are compared as EXACT strings, so preserve any leading zeros
#     that SAP uses ("0000123456" ≠ "123456").
#   • Reloaded automatically at every :15/:45 boundary — you can edit
#     this file mid-run without restarting the bot.
#   • You can also (or instead) set PRIORITY_VBELNS in .env as a
#     comma-separated list; both sources are merged and de-duplicated.
#
# Example (copy this file to priority.csv and edit):
1153420264
1153420262
1153406814
